This extension adds Jurassic World Evolution 3 modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]ACSE automatically installed.[/summary]

ACSE will be automatically downloaded and installed.

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]Epic[/*]
[*]Xbox[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]ACSE installs to the "Win64\ovldata" folder, recognised by an "ACSE" file.[/*]
[*]Root Game Folder mods with a "Win64" folder install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]ACSE mods with a "Main.ovl" file install to the "Win64\ovldata" folder.[/*]
[*]ACSE Localization mods with a "localised" folder install to the "Win64\ovldata\ACSE" folder.[/*]
[*]Movies mods with a ".webm" file install to the "Movies" folder.[/*]
[*]Ovldata Subfolder mods with an "ovldata" file install to the "Win64" folder.[/*]
[*]Saves mods with a ".blpr2" file install to the "%USERPROFILE%\Saved Games\Frontier Developments\Jurassic World Evolution 3\<User ID>\Saves" folder.[/*]
[*]Any other mod not described above installs to the game folder.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]Automatically downloads and installs [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/jurassicworldevolution3/mods/2]ACSE[/url]﻿, which is required by most mods.[/*]
[*]Includes a mod type to install mods to the game's root folder.[/*]
[/list]

[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for Jurassic World Evolution 3 mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

ACSE (mod loader):

This installer handles ACSE, not mods for it. It exists so users can install ACSE through Vortex, and mod authors normally never package this.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by a file named "ACSE" in the archive.

  Installs to: "Win64\ovldata"

  Common mistakes:
    - If you bundle ACSE inside your mod archive, Vortex treats the whole download as ACSE rather than as your mod. Ship the mod alone and list ACSE as a requirement.

========================================================================

Root / Game Folder Mods:

For mods laid out the same way the files appear inside the game folder. Vortex copies the matched folder and everything under it straight into the game.

[code]
MyRootMod.zip
└── Win64\
    └── ... files in their real relative locations
[/code]

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by a folder named "Win64", "Blueprints", "Islands", "TerrainSkirts" or "Movies" in the archive.

  Installs to: the game folder

  Common mistakes:
    - Zipping the folder that CONTAINS the game folders, instead of the game folders themselves, adds an extra level and misplaces every file.

========================================================================

ACSE Mods:

Lua mods that run under ACSE.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by any file named "Main.ovl".

  Installs to: "Win64\ovldata"

  Common mistakes:
    - The archive must contain "Main.ovl" - ACSE identifies mods by that file.

========================================================================

Localised:

Recognised when the archive contains a "localised" folder.

  Installs to: "Win64\ovldata\ACSE"

========================================================================

Movie / Cutscene Replacements:

Replacement video files, deployed into the game's movies folder.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by any file with the ".webm" extension.

  Installs to: "Movies"

  Common mistakes:
    - The replacement must keep the original file name, or the game will not pick it up.

========================================================================

OVL Data Mods:

Packed Cobra Engine content.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by any file named "ovldata".

  Installs to: "Win64"

========================================================================

Save Game Files:

Save files, deployed to the game's save folder.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by any file with the ".blpr2" or ".prk2" extensions.

  Installs to: "%USERPROFILE%\Saved Games\Frontier Developments\Jurassic World Evolution 3\<User ID>\Saves"

  Common mistakes:
    - Including an example save alongside a normal mod makes the archive install as a save.

========================================================================

Fallback Installer:

The catch-all. Any archive that matched none of the installers above lands here and is copied across unchanged.

[b][color=#ffff00]NOTE: Landing in the fallback installer is a signal your archive layout needs fixing.[/color][/b]

  Requirements:
    - Reaching this installer usually means the archive was not laid out in a way Vortex recognised.
    - Vortex shows the user a notification when a mod installs through the fallback.

  Common mistakes:
    - If your mod lands here unintentionally, re-check the layouts above - users will see a fallback warning and may report the mod as broken.

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine.
[/spoiler]

